{"name":"Soda Pop","hex":"#c3c67e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soda pop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several sweetened, carbonated beverages."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soda_pop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soda Pop (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Soda Pop\" is a song performed by Andrew Choi, Neckwav, Danny Chung, Kevin Woo, and SamUIL Lee as the fictional boy band the Saja Boys in the 2025 animated musical fantasy film KPop Demon Hunters. It was released on August 27, 2025, through Republic Records, as a promotional single for the film's soundtrack album. It was created by the writers Vince, Kush, and Chung and producers 24, Dominsuk, and Ian Eisendrath."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Saja_Boys_-_Soda_Pop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soda_Pop_(song)"},{"title":"...Baby One More Time (album)","blocks":[{"text":"...Baby One More Time is the debut studio album by American singer Britney Spears. It was released on January 12, 1999, by Jive Records. Spears had been a child performer on The All-New Mickey Mouse Club from 1993 to 1994, and was looking to expand her career as a teen singer. After being turned away by several record companies, Spears signed with Jive for a multi-album deal in 1997. She travelled to Sweden to collaborate with producers Max Martin and Rami Yacoub, who had been writing songs with producer Denniz Pop and others, for ...Baby One More Time. Their collaboration created a pop, bubblegum pop, dance-pop, and teen pop record, with Spears later saying that she felt excited when she heard it and knew it was going to be a hit record. The album was completed in June 1998."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28album%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/...Baby_One_More_Time_(album)"},{"title":"Soft drink","blocks":[{"text":"A soft drink is a class of beverage containing no alcohol, usually carbonated, and typically including added sweetener. Flavors can be natural, artificial or a mixture of the two. The sweetener may be a sugar, high-fructose corn syrup, fruit juice, a sugar substitute, or some combination of these. Soft drinks may also contain caffeine, colorings, preservatives and other ingredients. Soft drinks are called \"soft\" in contrast with \"hard\" alcoholic drinks and non-alcoholic drinks. Small amounts of alcohol may be present in a soft drink, but the alcohol content must be less than 0.5% of the total volume of the drink (ABV) in many countries and localities if the drink is to not be considered alcoholic. Examples of soft drinks include lemon-lime drinks, orange soda, cola, grape soda, cream soda, ginger ale and root beer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg/330px-Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_drink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d3/..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28International%29.png/250px-..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28International%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28International%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d3/..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28International%29.png/250px-..._Baby_One_More_Time_%28International%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A..._Baby_One_More_Time_(International).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Britney_Spears_%27Piece_of_Me%27_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_%2826906264843%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spears performing \"(You Drive Me) Crazy\" at her Las Vegas residency show, Britney: Piece of Me, in February 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritney_Spears_'Piece_of_Me'_-_Las_Vegas_IMG_6676_(26906264843)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Femme_Fatale_Vancouver_13.jpg/500px-Femme_Fatale_Vancouver_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Femme_Fatale_Vancouver_13.jpg/500px-Femme_Fatale_Vancouver_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spears and some of her dancers performing lead single \"...Baby One More Time\" during her 2011 Femme Fatale Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFemme_Fatale_Vancouver_13.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/016_Coca-Cola_vending_machine_at_Kyoto_Station%2C_Japan_-_%E3%82%B3%E3%82%AB%E3%82%B3%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A9_%E8%87%AA%E5%8B%95%E8%B2%A9%E5%A3%B2%E6%A9%9F.JPG/500px-016_Coca-Cola_vending_machin